# Prettier formats code here, not prose and not machine output.

node_modules/
dist/
build/

# Expo-generated, gitignored, and self-labelled "should not be edited". Prettier
# does not read .gitignore, so without these the format check trips on a file no
# human wrote and cannot fix by hand.
.expo/
**/expo-env.d.ts

# Markdown is hand-authored and hand-wrapped throughout this repo, with compact
# `|---|---|` tables and `*emphasis*`. Prettier rewrites both on sight, which
# would turn every docs edit into a reformatting diff and bury the actual
# change.
*.md

# NOTE — the token outputs that used to be listed here left with the design
# system (github.com/insolvia-ai/design-system): tokens.json, the generated
# tokens.ts, and the generated theme.css are all that repo's now, and its own
# .prettierignore carries the reasoning.
#
# What remains generated HERE is Cognito's managed-login branding,
# infra/modules/auth/managed-login-settings.json, written by
# tool/reconcile-cognito-branding.ts from the installed @insolvia-ai/tokens.
# It needs no entry: the root `format` script targets apps/insolvia_app,
# packages/insolvia_api_client and tool/, so nothing under infra/ is checked in
# the first place. `npm run tokens:check` is what guards that file, and it
# compares bytes — so if infra/ is ever added to the format target, this is the
# line that has to come back with it.
